          "item": {
            "@type": "NewsArticle",
            "headline": "Git Is Breaking Under the Weight of AI Coding Agents Flooding GitHub With Commits",
            "articleSection": "Job Evolution",
            "abstract": "The explosion of AI coding agents autonomously generating, committing, and merging code is pushing GitHub and the underlying Git version-control system to its architectural limits, with engineers warning the infrastructure was never designed for the volume or pace of machine-generated changes now hitting it. Developers report degraded performance, merge conflicts at unprecedented scale, and review queues that human engineers cannot keep up with. Industry observers say Git's decade-old design assumptions must be fundamentally rethought for an agentic coding world.",
            "url": "https://www.theregister.com/devops/2026/05/15/git-is-unprepared-for-the-ai-coding-tsunami/5241480",
            "publisher": {
              "@type": "NewsMediaOrganization",
              "name": "The AI Chronicle",
              "url": "https://theaichronicle.com",
              "logo": {
